llama: the loader copies a duplicate of a lazy tensor from the file and not through the mapping
Fold-into: upstream/loader

The defect

With LLAMA_LAZY_MODE_ON and no mmap load, load_all_data reads a tensor through the file mapping
when lazy.has() is true, and lazy.has() compares only the name. A tied output of qwen35 on a
device is a duplicate of token_embd.weight with the same name and a buffer of its own, thus the
loader copied it through the mapping. The lazy range has POSIX_MADV_RANDOM, thus that copy faulted
in one page at a time: the load of Qwen3.5 2B Q8_0 on HTP0 took 25.5 to 25.7 s against 5.0 to
5.4 s without the lazy mode, and the first decode 186 against 45 ms. On the host CPU with a cold
page cache the load took 14.3 s against 6.6 s.

The change

A tensor reads through the mapping only when it is lazy and has no data yet, that is the lazy
tensor itself. A duplicate with a buffer of its own reads from the file as in a load without the
lazy mode. With --drop-cache on the host the 2B loads in 1.1 to 3.0 s with the lazy mode and in
2.2 to 6.3 s without it (the box has a high load), and the logits hashes are the same.
test-lazy-embd covers the logits of the three loads.

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 with the patches of patches/series above this one.

Files:
    src/llama-model-loader.cpp
